  "title": "YouTube's View Count Tracking Update",
  "summary": "YouTube is introducing a new view count tracking method to align with platforms like Instagram and TikTok, which means creators may see their total view counts increase faster moving forward. The change comes a year after YouTube applied the same approach to Shorts videos.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "YouTube will count a view as soon as a video starts playing, aligning with Instagram and TikTok's methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The update will go into effect on August 24, 2027, potentially increasing creators' view counts.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "This change is part of a broader update to how views are counted across video formats.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
